  "labelNotes": "The p5 Power Supply Characteristics table is badly garbled in the dump; values were read with pdftotext -layout/-bbox. Several printed values appear in the dump only as footnote markers: Icc1 typ 21 mA ('[^21]'), Isb1 Com. 10 mA ('[^10]'), Isb2 Ind. 6 mA ('[^6]'). They are printed in the PDF and labelled. Columns are speed grades -8/-10/-20 with Min/Max each, and sub-rows Com./Ind./Auto.; all non-dash Max values are labelled MAX, typ.(2) rows TYP, in mA. Conditions: Icc 'Iout = 0 mA' -> IOUT = 0 mA (f = fmax is not numeric); 'f = 0' -> F = 0 Hz (unit Hz added by me). Distinct tuples only: Icc Ind -20 30 and Auto -20 45 duplicate Com/Ind values; Isb2 Auto 15 duplicates Isb1 Ind 15 (both F = 0 Hz, mA, MAX) so one label. Supply: there is no Recommended Operating Conditions table; the OPERATING RANGE table (p4) gives 2.4V-3.6V per grade (split MIN/MAX) and 3.3V +/- 10% for the 8 ns part (labelled 3.3 NOM; the +/-10% bounds are not printed numbers). I attached the row's Ambient Temperature as TA (Industrial and A1 rows give the same tuple; A3 is -40 to 125 C); doubtful whether that column counts as a row condition. The DC table headers 'VDD = 3.3V + 10%' / '2.4V-3.6V' repeat the range and are not labelled again. Leakage ILI -1/1 uA appears in both DC tables with identical values, labelled once; ILO excluded. Abs max: Vdd '-0.3 to 4.0' -> 4.0; Vterm 'Vdd + 0.5' skipped. Citations on value-only 'Auto.' lines span cells to be unique."
}